# Pull Requests

## Which repository

| Work | PR target repo |
|------|----------------|
| Code under `projects/<name>/` | That sub-project's GitHub repo |
| Template files at workspace root | This template repo |

## Title

- Format: `type(scope): subject` — same [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/) as commits and issues.
- **English**, imperative, concise.
- Do **not** put `#42` in the title; link issues in the body (`Fixes #42`).

## Body (six sections; 正文可用繁體中文)

1. **Summary** — required
2. **Changes** — required (bullet list)
3. **Testing** — required (what you ran)
4. **Screenshots / Demo** — required for UI changes; backend-only may use `N/A` or omit
5. **Related issues** — required when an issue exists (`Fixes #n` / `Closes #n`)
6. **Checklist** — required (lint, tests, CI)

Section headings in English; body text may be Traditional Chinese.

## Merge (recommended; follow repo GitHub settings)

- **Squash merge** into the default branch.
- Use the **PR title** as the squash commit message.
- Squash messages are the primary **changelog input** for releases (see rule `release`, skill `release-workflow`).
- **Delete branch** after merge when GitHub offers it.

## Review & CI

| Rule | Default |
|------|---------|
| Required approvals | **0** (solo); sub-projects may require 1+ in their rules or branch protection |
| CI | **Must pass** before merge |
| Checks | Per `.github/workflows/` — at minimum **lint** when a lint job exists (see `code-style`) |

Do not merge if required checks are failing unless the user explicitly accepts the risk.

## AI / GitHub MCP

| Allowed anytime | Only on explicit user request |
|-----------------|-------------------------------|
| Read PR, diff, CI/check status | Create PR, update PR body, request review, merge |
| Draft title + body in chat | Push branch (see `git-commits`) |

Default: present a PR draft first; create or update on GitHub only when asked (e.g. "開 PR", "update the PR").

**Never** merge a PR unless the user explicitly asks and CI/review rules are satisfied.

Copy `templates/github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` into sub-projects. See skill `github-pr-workflow`.
